WEBVTT

00:01.160 --> 00:03.879
No, I think your retainer is sexy.

00:04.960 --> 00:08.509
I do. You just gotta remember to clean it
after lunch.

00:08.680 --> 00:11.035
Hey, Jake,
how about you and me going out...?

00:11.200 --> 00:12.792
Okay, now I have a question for you.

00:12.960 --> 00:15.315
If I needed a lung
and your dad needed a lung...

00:15.480 --> 00:17.471
...who would you give your lung to?

00:18.280 --> 00:20.953
Well, now see,
I wouldn't have to think about it.

00:21.520 --> 00:24.353
Jake, I'm talking to you.
Don't give me the hand.

00:24.520 --> 00:26.715
Hang on. I'm talking to a girl.

00:27.720 --> 00:29.790
Sorry. Oh, no, that was nobody.

00:32.000 --> 00:34.912
That's it. Time to get a new kid.

00:35.320 --> 00:37.197
Hey, Alan,
you wanna catch a movie tonight?

00:37.360 --> 00:39.635
Can't. I am taking a lady
to the Hollywood Bowl...

00:39.800 --> 00:43.190
...for a romantic evening under the stars
with Michael Bublé...

00:43.360 --> 00:45.396
...and three runners-up
from &lt;i>American Idol.&lt;/i>

00:47.560 --> 00:49.312
What's in the bag, a noose?

00:50.280 --> 00:53.238
No, it's a picnic basket.
Fried chicken, bottle of merlot...

00:53.400 --> 00:55.994
...and my autograph hound
in case I get lucky.

00:57.120 --> 01:01.272
- Why don't you take Jake to the movies?
- No, I don't like him anymore.

01:01.920 --> 01:04.070
Okay, then why don't you take
one of your many...?

01:04.240 --> 01:06.515
Oh, let's call them girlfriends.

01:07.160 --> 01:08.149
Yeah, I could...

01:08.320 --> 01:10.595
...but, after the movie,
I bring them back here...

01:10.760 --> 01:12.796
...after I get them here,
I get them upstairs.

01:12.960 --> 01:16.236
After I get them upstairs,
I gotta get them to go home.

01:16.840 --> 01:19.479
It just doesn't seem
worth the effort anymore.

01:19.640 --> 01:22.757
It's possible you might enjoy your dates
if you went out with women...

01:22.920 --> 01:27.072
...who are capable of using their head
other than a place to rest their ankles.

01:32.400 --> 01:34.118
What are you saying?

01:35.120 --> 01:36.712
Too subtle?

01:36.880 --> 01:39.997
I'm saying you might have a better time
if you were seeing someone...

01:40.160 --> 01:44.199
...who had a fully formed personality
or was even remotely age-appropriate.

01:44.360 --> 01:47.158
- Define "age appropriate."
- Forty.

01:47.320 --> 01:48.833
Are you out of your mind?

01:49.840 --> 01:52.035
Come on, Charlie.
The woman I'm seeing now is 39.

01:52.200 --> 01:54.919
We have a wonderful time
because we have so much in common.

01:55.080 --> 01:56.911
We can talk, we can share,
we can laugh.

01:57.080 --> 02:01.949
Talking, sharing and laughing is fine
but what about her ears?

02:03.000 --> 02:06.117
- What about them?
- Ears never stop growing, Alan.

02:06.280 --> 02:09.477
And I like a nice, taut lobe.

02:10.360 --> 02:12.351
This conversation is over.

02:12.600 --> 02:13.589
I will see you later.

02:13.760 --> 02:15.876
Why do you think old ladies
wear big earrings?

02:17.240 --> 02:19.629
To make their ears look smaller.

02:20.680 --> 02:23.399
Like I'm the only one who's noticed.

02:26.280 --> 02:28.111
&lt;i>I'd like to make a toast to my wife.&lt;/i>

02:28.280 --> 02:31.158
&lt;i>Darling, you've given me&lt;/i>
&lt;i>the happiest 20 years of my life.&lt;/i>

02:31.600 --> 02:34.398
Why? Was she in a coma?

02:35.080 --> 02:37.958
&lt;i>I can 't imagine living without you.&lt;/i>
&lt;i>You complete me.&lt;/i>

02:38.960 --> 02:41.633
Bet she's got a set of ears on her.

02:42.600 --> 02:44.716
Oh, yeah.

02:45.160 --> 02:48.232
You could swat flies with those things.

03:03.560 --> 03:05.039
Hey, pal.

03:05.440 --> 03:07.670
It's just you and me tonight, huh?

03:08.880 --> 03:10.836
Yeah, I know how you feel.

03:11.400 --> 03:12.958
There's a lot of fish in the sea...

03:13.120 --> 03:15.998
...but after you catch them
and eat them, then what?

03:17.600 --> 03:21.149
Damn straight. It's not worth the hassle.

03:23.000 --> 03:25.958
My mistake.
Didn't know you had a date.

03:27.520 --> 03:30.637
If you two don't have plans, why don't
you fly to the Hollywood Bowl...

03:30.800 --> 03:33.234
...and take a crap on my brother?

03:40.600 --> 03:44.354
Really? I dreamt about you too.
What was your dream?

03:44.640 --> 03:46.995
We were on a train in a tunnel?

03:47.800 --> 03:49.836
Sounds kind of boring.

03:50.960 --> 03:52.473
It means what?

03:54.120 --> 03:56.395
Oh, hey, you're up early.

03:56.560 --> 03:58.437
No way.

03:58.600 --> 04:02.195
I am not just getting home.
I couldn't sleep so I went for a walk.

04:02.680 --> 04:05.513
Dad, a little privacy, please?

04:05.680 --> 04:08.399
Okay, I just didn't want you to get
the wrong idea.

04:08.640 --> 04:12.599
I'm confused. If I'm in the train,
how can I be the train?

04:18.000 --> 04:19.797
At least he's not the tunnel.

04:22.320 --> 04:23.799
Hi.

04:24.400 --> 04:26.311
I'm just getting in.

04:28.080 --> 04:29.354
Yeah, I can see that.

04:29.520 --> 04:31.590
Didn't get much sleep last night.

04:33.840 --> 04:37.549
- And yet I feel totally rested.
- Good for you.

04:38.480 --> 04:42.519
I mean, rested but spent.

04:43.480 --> 04:44.799
Gotcha.

04:44.960 --> 04:49.192
I mean, not so much spent
as happily depleted.

04:50.200 --> 04:53.112
- Joyously bereft of...
- I get it. You got laid.

04:54.720 --> 04:58.838
And Michael Bublé's autograph.

05:02.480 --> 05:04.357
Congratulations.

05:04.800 --> 05:07.553
So how was your evening?

05:18.640 --> 05:20.551
You know, I talked to Donna about you.

05:21.320 --> 05:23.231
- Donna?
- The woman I was with last night.

05:23.400 --> 05:27.313
Oh, yeah, yeah. You talk, you share,
you laugh. Kiss my ass.

05:28.440 --> 05:31.034
Anyway, turns out she has a friend
who's newly single.

05:31.200 --> 05:33.998
- And I suggested...
- A blind date?

05:34.160 --> 05:37.232
Forget it. Charlie Harper does not go
on blind dates.

05:37.680 --> 05:39.796
- He doesn't?
- No, he doesn't.

05:43.520 --> 05:45.351
Can't we ask him?

05:46.760 --> 05:48.876
Don't bother. I know what he'll say.

05:49.840 --> 05:52.513
Okay, but does he have to say it
in the third person?

05:53.360 --> 05:56.272
Look, I don't need anybody to get me
dates. I can get my own dates.

05:56.440 --> 05:59.830
But you were complaining that the
women you go out with don't fulfill you.

06:00.000 --> 06:02.673
Donna's friend is beautiful.
She's accomplished, she's smart.

06:02.840 --> 06:05.638
- How old is she?
- I think around 40.

06:05.800 --> 06:07.791
Hello.

06:11.400 --> 06:15.439
- Still with the ears?
- It's not just ears.

06:15.600 --> 06:17.795
Women that age have a lot of baggage.

06:17.960 --> 06:20.520
Right. And you've just got a carryon.

06:25.360 --> 06:27.590
Think about this.
What if I meet this woman?

06:27.760 --> 06:30.320
I like her, she likes me,
we get married and settle down?

06:31.240 --> 06:34.755
We're both 40 now.
In 20 years, I'm gonna be 60.

06:34.920 --> 06:36.592
And do you know how old
she's gonna be?

06:38.960 --> 06:41.633
- Sixty?
- I rest my case.

06:47.960 --> 06:50.554
- That was nice, huh?
- I guess.

06:51.760 --> 06:54.638
My ear's still a little soggy.

06:55.000 --> 06:56.433
Sorry.

06:56.600 --> 07:00.593
So, Deedee, is that short for anything?

07:01.080 --> 07:03.833
- Like what?
- I don't know.

07:06.800 --> 07:08.438
No, it's just a nickname.

07:10.080 --> 07:13.038
- What's your real name?
- Sissy.

07:13.680 --> 07:15.318
Sissy, huh?

07:15.480 --> 07:18.153
I guess that means
you throw a ball like a girl.

07:18.320 --> 07:19.673
I am a girl.

07:21.800 --> 07:23.358
Right.

07:24.160 --> 07:28.073
- Is Charlie short for anything?
- Charles.

07:29.160 --> 07:30.991
That's not really shorter, is it?

07:34.440 --> 07:36.396
Excuse me.

07:37.320 --> 07:40.710
Why? Did you fart?

07:44.560 --> 07:46.437
No, you hang up first.

07:46.600 --> 07:48.033
Okay, on three.

07:48.200 --> 07:50.760
One, two, three.

07:50.920 --> 07:54.230
You didn't hang up, did you?
Me neither.

07:58.360 --> 08:00.510
Okay, set it up.

08:00.880 --> 08:02.313
What?

08:03.120 --> 08:05.634
The blind date with the old chick. I'm in.

08:08.880 --> 08:10.438
What?

08:13.920 --> 08:17.879
- Alan, let's go.
- Relax, we've got plenty of time.

08:18.040 --> 08:20.190
I just don't wanna be late.

08:20.360 --> 08:22.635
I can't believe it.
You're nervous about a date.

08:22.800 --> 08:26.236
Of course I'm nervous.
What am I gonna talk to her about?

08:26.400 --> 08:29.233
I haven't gone out with
a 40-year-old woman since high school.

08:32.720 --> 08:35.712
Charlie, that's the great thing about
seeing someone your own age.

08:35.880 --> 08:37.632
There's always something to talk about.

08:37.800 --> 08:40.075
What you've been through,
she's been through.

08:40.560 --> 08:43.074
Oh, I hardly think so.

08:43.240 --> 08:45.595
All right, point taken.
But she's a fascinating woman.

08:45.760 --> 08:49.116
She's a municipal court judge,
she teaches law at UCLA.

08:49.280 --> 08:50.838
Oh, man, you didn't tell me that.

08:51.000 --> 08:53.036
- Does that make a difference?
- Big difference.

08:53.200 --> 08:56.749
The smarter the girl, the harder it is
to blow smoke up her ass.

09:02.600 --> 09:04.318
You know, I'm already regretting this.

09:04.720 --> 09:06.676
And for good reason.
Let's just call it off.

09:06.840 --> 09:08.398
No, no, no, it's too late for that.

09:08.560 --> 09:11.518
Just relax and, I don't know,
be yourself.

09:11.680 --> 09:14.831
And by "yourself,"
I mean someone else entirely.

09:15.000 --> 09:16.069
Anything else?

09:16.240 --> 09:18.800
Well, as long we've opened
this particular can of worms...

09:18.960 --> 09:21.599
...you might wanna rethink
the bowling shirt.

09:23.600 --> 09:24.919
- Why?
- Well, as I said...

09:25.080 --> 09:26.752
...she's a judge and a law professor.

09:26.920 --> 09:29.912
And, let's be honest, you don't bowl.

09:31.280 --> 09:32.554
All right, I'll go change.

09:32.720 --> 09:34.517
- And Charlie?
- Yeah?

09:34.680 --> 09:37.399
While you're at it, why don't we go
for the big-boy pants.

09:40.480 --> 09:41.959
Fine.

09:45.280 --> 09:47.919
- Oh, there they are.
- Hang on, hang on, hang on.

09:48.280 --> 09:49.429
Which one's mine?

09:50.600 --> 09:53.717
- The one on the right.
- Wow, she's 40?

09:54.320 --> 09:57.039
She has the ears of a 20-year-old.

09:59.160 --> 10:00.639
Come on.

10:01.440 --> 10:03.192
You think she had them done?

10:04.760 --> 10:07.320
Sorry we're late.
Charlie couldn't decide what to wear.

10:07.480 --> 10:09.550
Oh, I think he looks very nice.

10:09.720 --> 10:11.312
- Thank you.
- Charlie, this is Donna.

10:11.480 --> 10:13.038
- Hi, how are you?
- Hi.

10:13.200 --> 10:14.349
This is my friend, Linda.

10:14.720 --> 10:16.517
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you too.

10:16.680 --> 10:19.752
- I've heard a lot about you.
- And I've heard a lot about you too.

10:20.240 --> 10:22.800
And, I gotta say,
I am pleasantly surprised.

10:24.080 --> 10:25.479
Really? How so?

10:26.000 --> 10:29.675
Well, Alan tells me
you're a judge and a professor...

10:29.840 --> 10:33.833
...and, quite frankly,
I wasn't expecting someone so...

10:34.520 --> 10:36.590
So, what, Charlie?

10:38.400 --> 10:39.958
Yummy.

10:47.400 --> 10:49.231
That was wrong, wasn't it?

10:50.680 --> 10:52.352
Yes, that was wrong.

10:53.080 --> 10:56.595
What I meant was,
I was expecting you to be...

10:56.760 --> 10:59.513
...more, you know, dry.

11:00.720 --> 11:04.110
But you're not.
You're actually kind of moist.

11:09.040 --> 11:10.792
Oh, good Lord.

11:12.720 --> 11:16.076
You know what? You know what?
I think I'd like to start over.

11:16.240 --> 11:18.993
- Hi, I'm Charlie.
- Linda.

11:19.160 --> 11:20.434
Hi, Linda.

11:20.600 --> 11:23.160
I gotta tell you,
I have never met a judge before.

11:23.320 --> 11:24.958
You know, voluntarily.

11:33.720 --> 11:37.315
- Better?
- Anything's better than "moist."

11:42.360 --> 11:44.112
So how do you and Donna
know each other?

11:44.280 --> 11:46.111
Oh, well, we met in the church choir.

11:46.280 --> 11:48.271
We found our kids
were in the same preschool.

11:48.440 --> 11:51.557
Next thing, we're on the carnival
committee, doing the bake sale.

11:51.720 --> 11:54.393
Which reminds me, I'm supposed to be
snack mom next Tuesday.

11:54.560 --> 11:55.879
- Can you switch?
- No problem.

11:56.040 --> 11:57.712
Thanks.

12:03.000 --> 12:04.718
I got nothing.

12:06.360 --> 12:08.157
Hey, hey. Why don't we order
some drinks?

12:08.880 --> 12:10.233
- Just iced tea for me.
- Me too.

12:10.400 --> 12:13.551
- Charlie, you want iced tea?
- Why on Earth would I want iced tea?

12:16.000 --> 12:18.309
Because you don't drink alcohol
during the daytime.

12:19.120 --> 12:22.396
Oh, right, of course not.

12:22.560 --> 12:23.993
Iced tea, rocks, water back.

12:25.360 --> 12:28.238
- Excuse me, miss?
- Yes, can I help...? Charlie?

12:29.800 --> 12:32.075
Oh, hey. Hi.

12:32.400 --> 12:35.631
- How come you never called me?
- Well...

12:39.000 --> 12:41.275
Funny story. Long story.

12:41.440 --> 12:42.634
Tell you later.

12:42.800 --> 12:45.917
- Can we get four iced teas, please?
- I'll be right back.

12:52.360 --> 12:56.876
- Old friend?
- Yeah, you know, church choir, bake sale.

12:59.280 --> 13:01.714
You may not wanna drink the iced tea.

13:06.880 --> 13:09.917
You know, Alan, I gotta hand it to you,
Linda is really something.

13:10.080 --> 13:11.877
Yeah, yeah. She's terrific.

13:12.040 --> 13:14.793
- But let me ask you something.
- Sure.

13:14.960 --> 13:18.873
What in God's name possessed you
to talk about pornography?

13:20.600 --> 13:23.319
- Hey, she started it.
- She wasn't talking about pornography.

13:23.480 --> 13:26.790
She was talking about constitutional law
and the First Amendment.

13:26.960 --> 13:30.714
- Which includes pornography.
- Yes, it does.

13:30.880 --> 13:34.429
But it does not include
your favorite actresses, top 10 DVDs...

13:34.600 --> 13:36.716
...or your beefs
about the bonus features.

13:37.680 --> 13:40.035
I just pointed out that the bloopers,
though funny...

13:40.200 --> 13:41.838
...are really more of a turnoff.

13:45.280 --> 13:47.919
Hello? Yeah, yeah. Hi, Donna.

13:48.080 --> 13:51.197
Charlie and I were just talking
about what a nice time we had.

13:51.840 --> 13:53.478
Okay, I'm sorry.

13:54.680 --> 13:55.908
I'm sorry.

13:57.080 --> 13:58.638
Ask her if Linda likes me.

13:58.800 --> 14:00.870
Hang on. You're kidding, right?

14:01.040 --> 14:02.951
Come on, chicks talk to each other.

14:04.800 --> 14:07.553
Donna, would you please tell my brother
what you just told me?

14:07.720 --> 14:08.914
Here.

14:09.920 --> 14:11.911
Hey, Donna. Talk to me.

14:14.960 --> 14:18.873
I see. Okay, well,
thanks for the heads up.

14:19.040 --> 14:20.758
Linda didn't like me.

14:21.440 --> 14:23.078
Go figure.

14:24.640 --> 14:27.200
I told her not to drink the iced tea.

14:31.320 --> 14:34.232
That's what I heard.
Danny Sholander likes Jennifer Denapoli.

14:34.840 --> 14:36.159
Hi.

14:39.320 --> 14:41.231
Really? He's gay?

14:41.400 --> 14:43.231
Does he know that?

14:44.160 --> 14:46.879
You gotta get me another crack at her.

14:47.040 --> 14:49.395
- What?
- I need to see her again.

14:49.560 --> 14:52.279
- See who?
- Linda. I can't let it end this way.

14:52.440 --> 14:55.989
- Let what end? It was a lunch.
- No, no, no. It was more than a lunch.

14:56.160 --> 15:00.233
It was a test. Is Charlie Harper capable
of stepping up to quality women?

15:00.400 --> 15:02.789
Oh, God, we're back to third person.

15:03.200 --> 15:06.397
Alan, I am tired of having
meaningless sex with hot pinheads.

15:06.560 --> 15:08.790
What a coincidence.
I'm tired of hearing about it.

15:10.000 --> 15:12.560
Linda's smart, Linda's sophisticated,
Linda's successful.

15:12.720 --> 15:16.110
- Linda doesn't like you.
- She will. I can make her.

15:16.280 --> 15:19.272
You just need to tell Donna to tell Linda
to give me another chance.

15:19.440 --> 15:21.954
Fine, I'll pass her a note
during study hall.

15:22.120 --> 15:25.032
Hey, hey, hey,
don't belittle my feelings.

15:25.200 --> 15:27.668
I'm in a very sensitive place
and I will kick your ass.

15:28.720 --> 15:32.429
Look. Come on, Charlie. So you
struck out with a woman. It happens.

15:32.600 --> 15:34.670
Believe me, it happens.

15:35.520 --> 15:39.115
When it does, the best thing to do
is to pick yourself up, dust yourself off...

15:39.280 --> 15:42.352
...and curse God for making you
the way you are.

15:42.840 --> 15:47.311
All right, forget it. I don't need you.
I'll call her myself.

15:53.120 --> 15:55.509
Sorry about the "curse God" stuff...

15:55.680 --> 15:58.399
...but we both know
I'm not your best work.

16:02.560 --> 16:05.597
Yeah, hi, can I speak
to Judge Linda Harris please?

16:05.760 --> 16:07.398
Charlie Harper.

16:07.920 --> 16:10.275
Yes, again.

16:11.200 --> 16:13.191
All right, fine,
put me through to voice mail.

16:13.360 --> 16:16.511
Banging a judge won't get you out
of jury duty. Believe me, I've tried.

16:17.600 --> 16:19.989
No, no, no. Quiet.

16:20.600 --> 16:22.989
Yeah, hi, Linda. It's Charlie again.

16:23.160 --> 16:25.720
I just want you to know
that this will be my last message.

16:26.080 --> 16:29.709
I figure three's a charm,
four is a restraining order.

16:30.400 --> 16:32.277
Look who I'm telling.

16:33.280 --> 16:35.748
Anyway, I know we didn't get off
on the right foot.

16:35.920 --> 16:39.833
I'm not used to spending time with
such a remarkable, accomplished woman.

16:40.000 --> 16:41.718
Keep shoveling.

16:44.960 --> 16:48.748
And it's true. I've lived
a certain kind of life up until now.

16:48.920 --> 16:52.799
I'm not saying that I'm proud of it,
but I'm not ashamed of it either.

16:52.960 --> 16:55.633
Why else would you have videotaped
most of it?

16:57.800 --> 16:59.791
I'm begging you.

17:01.520 --> 17:04.796
So if you wanna call me back,
call me back.

17:04.960 --> 17:08.077
If not, well, have a nice life.

17:08.240 --> 17:11.994
But it would be a nicer life
if you called me.

17:13.440 --> 17:17.274
Wow, I never thought
I'd see Charlie Harper on his knees.

17:17.440 --> 17:18.555
You know, figuratively.

17:23.040 --> 17:25.429
Can we please talk about me
in the first person?

17:26.000 --> 17:27.797
What's this broad got that's so special?

17:28.320 --> 17:31.517
- A brain.
- What are you gonna do with a brain?

17:32.760 --> 17:34.557
It doesn't matter. She'll never call me.

17:34.720 --> 17:36.711
Oh, don't talk like that.

17:36.880 --> 17:39.030
Because she's smart and successful
doesn't mean...

17:39.200 --> 17:41.953
...she's not damaged enough
to go out with you.

17:43.720 --> 17:45.438
Thanks, Berta. That means a lot.

17:52.800 --> 17:54.631
Hello?

17:55.200 --> 17:57.555
No, Jake's not here.
Try him at his mom's house.

18:00.800 --> 18:03.917
- Where you going?
- I don't know.

18:04.080 --> 18:07.516
Someplace where the bottles are full
and the women are empty.

18:08.120 --> 18:11.556
&lt;i>And skies are not cloudy all day&lt;/i>

18:14.680 --> 18:18.229
Fifty-dollar fine, time served.
Call the next case.

18:18.400 --> 18:21.198
Case number 1217-07.

18:21.360 --> 18:25.035
Charles Harper, charged with drunk
and disorderly, resisting arrest.

18:25.600 --> 18:27.272
Charlie?

18:28.160 --> 18:30.833
Oh, hey.

18:31.200 --> 18:32.758
Small world, huh?

18:34.400 --> 18:35.992
Approach the bench, please.

18:37.040 --> 18:39.270
Excuse me. I think this is personal.

18:43.080 --> 18:46.709
Please tell me you did not get yourself
arrested just so you could see me.

18:50.920 --> 18:52.911
You got me.

18:53.080 --> 18:55.435
Charlie, what am I going to do with you?

18:56.160 --> 19:01.188
Have dinner with me. Otherwise,
we're looking at a crime spree here.

19:02.640 --> 19:05.074
All right, one dinner.

19:05.240 --> 19:07.117
- Now step back.
- Yes, ma'am.

19:09.120 --> 19:11.270
- How do you plead?
- Guilty, Your Honor.

19:11.440 --> 19:12.873
- Is this a first offense?
- Yes.

19:13.040 --> 19:15.998
- All right, $500 fine.
- Five hundred dollars? Last time...

19:16.160 --> 19:18.310
- Last time?
- Thank you, Your Honor.

19:19.360 --> 19:22.955
- Next case.
- Case number 1217-08.

19:23.120 --> 19:27.272
- Heidi Jones, charged with solicitation.
- Hey, Charlie.

19:36.520 --> 19:39.239
- Thanks for picking me up, Alan.
- Where's your car?

19:40.400 --> 19:43.676
- Good question.
- Oh, Charlie...

19:43.840 --> 19:47.913
Yeah, we just got my uncle out of jail.
It was cool. I saw a real pimp.

19:48.520 --> 19:52.195
- Well, I hope you learned a lesson here.
- I sure did.

19:52.360 --> 19:55.113
- What was that lesson?
- Lf a woman won't return your calls...

19:55.280 --> 19:58.670
...get drunk, get arrested,
then lie through your teeth.

19:58.840 --> 20:00.512
That's it? That's what you learned?

20:00.680 --> 20:05.879
Well, also, if your cellmate wants your
bologna sandwich, just give it to him.

20:07.120 --> 20:09.634
Okay, I'll be your pimp
if you'll be my beyotch.

20:09.800 --> 20:13.190
- Jake, that's enough with the phone.
- Nobody. What were you saying?

20:14.920 --> 20:16.558
Hey.

20:17.360 --> 20:19.590
I'd have kept the phone
and tossed the kid.

20:45.280 --> 20:47.271
Subtitles by
SDI Media Group

20:47.440 --> 20:49.431
[ENGLISH]
